(NATIVECAM CHIP-LOAD LADDER: 7 slots with 1/4in Upcut End Mill in hardwood, from below the end-mill)
(chart's chip loads to above them. A REAL CUT: use scrap.)
(Scrap at least 5.875 x 5 in and 0.75 in thick, clamped clear of the slots, with a straight front)
(edge.)
(Zero X and Y at the scrap's front-left corner, and Z on its top as for any job. Each slot plunges in)
(front of the scrap and cuts 0.125 in deep into it from the front edge; rung 1 is on the left.)
(Listen to each rung and keep its chips: the recording sheet lists each rung's feed, speed and chip)
(load.)
